#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:5
#: 40efc74acbc242fa9205d61b02b41f45
msgid "Telemetry Forwarding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:7
#: 03a0dd54b86a41c7824e6678d5225cc8
msgid "A key feature of MAVProxy is its ability to forward the messages from your UAV over the network via UDP to multiple other ground station software on other devices. For example: you can run a ground station on a laptop next to your antenna and forward via wifi to a smartphone/tablet which lets you easily relocate to launch into wind before heading back to your fixed antenna. You can also use it to send telemetry data to a friend acting as spotter several kilometers away (via 4G vpn) during a longer flight so that he could monitor the entire flight and determine where to look to find the aircraft in flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:21
#: ac3d3a1db4b548cb90188324a517211a
msgid "To forward the MAVLink data over the network including to a local program on your PC you simply need to add some extra parameters when starting MAVProxy via the command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:26
#: e5ffe91503b64230b5d0d12bca766b20
msgid "Local Forwarding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:28
#: d64e1bfab4134def9edbb2fcfa155678
msgid "To connect with a local ground station software (such as Mission Planner or QGC) start MAVProxy under Linux with the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:35
#: ee3d9241908e4f0eaf28a94afbd46b0b
msgid "an abbreviated version also works:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:41
#: d44154f56ac945769f51d6e4c04d8403
msgid "since MAVProxy will auto-connect to the autopilot on the Linux PC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:43
#: 4f30b29b8383486b94ea2b300096b924
msgid "For a Windows PC, start a command prompt and enter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:49
#: 83ef2f31d7f54a2096131fbe640e928c
msgid "where COMx is the com port to which the autopilot is attached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:51
#: 1c4dac3b087448e1a8cbaf1541849186
msgid "Then open the ground station software and select a UDP connection on port 14550. It should then connect to your UAV."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:55
#: 8c817404bd1a44cea2d9320f2d70611a
msgid "Forwarding to Remotes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:57
#: f423608b9356467eabc70db95aad1bec
msgid "While MAVProxy also has the capability of forwarding using TCP, it is not recommended, since network delays can cause long lags if joystick control is being used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:59
#: 6a38275d7d994a83a4704646bb5d2827
msgid "Finally, you can add the IP address of any computer to forward the telemetry stream onwards to other ground stations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:62
#: bbeca26d49614ab399365d65ccb607ef
msgid "On the local network/wifi you will need to ensure there is no firewall on the client PC stopping the incoming stream to your ground station software."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:65
#: be1cb95775df41b6a4e1d9c4064c7976
msgid "Add - -out *destination IP address*:14550 to the end of the MAVProxy command. You can add as many separate - -out parameters as you want depending on how many extra ground stations you are running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/forwarding.rst:68
#: 5deda27d86d74120a0ef991ba85df2fe
msgid "Set each ground station to listen for UDP packets on port 14550 and, again, make sure its firewall is not blocking incoming traffic on UDP port 14550."
msgstr ""
